WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Speaker 1: the continued bad news for&nbsp;
the failed former president Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.180
in an appeals court now says the Department of&nbsp;
Justice can resume its criminal probe of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.580
classified documents that were obtained at Mar&nbsp;
a Lago. Remember, once that search warrant was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:21.600
executed and the documents were taken, seized, the&nbsp;
Trump side said, we need a special master. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.220
medical documents in there. There's privileged&nbsp;
documents in there. Special master is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.700
look at all of it and, you know, classified,&nbsp;
declassified, just a complete and total mess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.800
We are now moving beyond that. As CNN reports,&nbsp;
a federal appeals court is allowing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.080
Justice Department to continue looking at those&nbsp;
documents marked classified seized from Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:46.740
The emergency intervention upends a trial judge's&nbsp;
order over those documents that had blocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:53.820
federal investigators work on the documents and&nbsp;
is a strong rebuke of the Trump team's attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.460
suggest, without evidence, that materials were&nbsp;
somehow declassified. Remember what happened?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.840
The special master said, Listen. If you're going&nbsp;
to make this argument about classification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.160
then make it and we're going to move on very&nbsp;
quickly if you don't, because the special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:16.500
master said, which I told you two days ago,&nbsp;
you give me a document that says Top secret.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.440
And you don't present any evidence that it&nbsp;
was declassified. That's it. Essentially a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.900
cut the crap moment. And that is exactly what is&nbsp;
going on here. The ruling was issued by a three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:34.860
judge panel of the 11th U.S. Circuit Court of&nbsp;
Appeals. Two of the three judges were nominated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:42.840
by Donald Trump. This is supposed to be quite&nbsp;
a conservative court. And it really goes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:48.900
show that the arguments Trump was making in&nbsp;
public were completely and totally absurd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:58.200
Perhaps the funniest line from the entire thing&nbsp;
is, quote, For our part, we cannot discern why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:06.540
the plaintiff would have an individual interest&nbsp;
in or need for any of the 100 documents with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:12.720
classification markings. And that sort of says it&nbsp;
all. We can't figure that out as well. It was for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.180
Trump's memoirs. He doesn't read or write. Trump&nbsp;
wanted to review the documents. He doesn't read or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.980
write. They were for Trump's library. The library&nbsp;
is not even something Trump is really thinking of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.660
according to many insiders. There's just no&nbsp;
reasonable explanation other than bad ones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.760
He wanted to sell them. He wanted to use them as&nbsp;
leverage. Horrible, horrible things that border&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.460
on treason. The judges couldn't understand that&nbsp;
either. So the investigation continues. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:43.620
is now an indictment watch taking place. We'll&nbsp;
see where we are another month or two from now.

